        "original_id": "6b986e88-c5f6-56a7-ad00-e57fd5d5f5b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wolfgang Wagner, Roy Spencer\n- Organizations: Remote Sensing, Vienna University of Technology, University of Alabama in Huntsville, NASA\n- Products: Advanced Microwave Scanning Radiometer (AMSR-E), Aqua satellite\n- Events: Wolfgang Wagner's resignation, publication criticism\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Warren Spencer was born on December 20, 1955.\n- Roy Spencer is a meteorologist and a principal research scientist at the University of Alabama in Huntsville.\n- Roy Spencer is the U.S. Science Team leader for the Advanced Microwave Scanning Radiometer (AMSR-E) on NASA's Aqua satellite.\n- Wolfgang Wagner of the Vienna University of Technology was the founding editor-in-chief of Remote Sensing until September 2, 2011.\n- On September 2, 2011, Wolfgang Wagner resigned from Remote Sensing over the journal's publication of a paper co-authored by Roy Spencer.\n- Roy Spencer's paper in Remote Sensing received significant criticism from other scientists soon after its publication.",
